                        "review": "Disgaea is a title that means a lot to me.  It was introduced to me right after getting my hands on La Pucelle: Tactics on the PS2 back around 2003 and further expanded my view on the strategy RPGs and its lore.  Without either, NIS/A as a company would likely have not been introduced to me as fondly as it may or may not have been and I would not have participated in a lot of games that I believe are very dear to me to this day.\n\nThat said, this isn't the first version of the original that I would recommend against.  While this is a little more competent than the Disgaea DS version, it has similar undertones of being phoned in and not very complete.  There are numerous bugs that have been reported, mostly on AMD platforms, and gamedev and bugfixing has long since ceased.  That alone should be enough of a reason for people to steer clear.  Worse still, there are no real options for comparison for the original entry in the series that are native to PC unless you delve into emulation.\n\nThough, speaking of Complete...If you're interested in this title at all and wish to play the best and most modern version, I would highly suggest looking into Disgaea 1 Complete on another platform.  Why they haven't taken the time to port that version onto Steam after all this time is anyone's guess but NIS/A hasn't exactly been a company I put a lot of faith in almost a quarter of a century down the road.  Any of the Complete titles in the Disgaea series are probably worth your time but be aware that as you go up the numbers that the games and the plots the use may begin to wear on you.  After about 4 or 5, I would say that's the cutoff for enjoyment for most people and likely where it began to get stale for the devs.  \n\nDisgaea itself seems something of a breakout hit for the company that I believe they never could have expected and their handling of this success is something of a mixed bag.  I certainly appreciate certain games that we've received in the franchise and the fact that the original wasn't the only title in the franchise, but the efforts didn't come without a few missed shots and this port is one of them.",
